<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick VII, Count of Toggenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1436</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Frederick VII of Toggenburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick VII was the last Count of Toggenburg, ruling a large territory in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> that stretched from the Toggenburg valley to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prattigau">Prättigau</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/davos">Davos</a>. He allied with both Zürich and Schwyz, and when he died without heirs in 1436 their rival claims to his lands led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-zurich-war">Old Zürich War</a> of 1440–1446. His subjects in Davos and the Prättigau formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-the-ten-jurisdictions">League of the Ten Jurisdictions</a> to protect their rights.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-vii-count-of-toggenburg.jpg" alt="Frederick VII, Count of Toggenburg" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friderici_VII_Toggenburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
